{"kind":"request","text":"Claude: make ordinary staleness quiet and world-staleness loud on the default read surfaces. Since the staleness relaxation merged (23c4c759), ordinary reasoning staleness blocks nothing — it honestly marks history whose bases moved — yet 1,111 of 1,168 artifacts and most closed commitments now carry the flag, so the default status and work views print a warning on nearly every row. A flare that fires everywhere carries no information and teaches readers to ignore the one that does (describes_superseded_world). Rebalance the presentation only; change no fold semantics.","body":{"conditions":"1) Default gs status output and the MCP status/work views summarize ordinary staleness (for example as counts per lane) instead of flagging every row, while world-staleness (describes_superseded_world) and retired-basis conditions remain individually visible wherever they occur. 2) No information loss: explicit modes (gs status --all / --json, work stale=include/only) still expose per-record staleness exactly as today. 3) The distinction between ordinary reasoning staleness and world-staleness is stated in the status reference documentation, in plain English per ISO 24495-1. 4) Deterministic tests pin both the default presentation and the explicit-detail presentation, and breaking the summarization turns a test red. Implement on a request/\u003cslug\u003e branch, publish exact-head artifacts per the discipline, and request independent review from codex.","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}